{
  "0": "Interaction mechanism: in all four categories, replace the scorer's user-item dot product with a jointly learned diagonal bilinear product, sum_d((1+0.1*tanh(a_d))*h_d*e_id), initializing a=0. This starts at the original compatibility and allows modest dimension reweighting without a separate predictor. Preserve GRU topology, inputs, history readout, loss and optimizer. Update the predictor writer to restore the scoring parameters; retain one model per category.",
  "1": "Learning objective: in all four categories, use L=L_existing+0.1*mean(softplus(s_negative-s_positive)), using only the existing sampled positive-negative pairs and masking padding. The auxiliary pairwise term may improve ranking against competitive negatives while retaining the original prediction objective. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU, scoring/readout, optimizer, sampling, scheduler and batch/epoch settings; retain one model per category.",
  "2": "Sequence modeling: in all four categories, cap each causal input history at its 30 most recent nonpadding interactions, preserving chronological order and existing targets. Apply the same cap during training and prediction, including the predictor writer. Shorter context may reduce interference from stale preferences and recurrent computation. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU topology, interest readout, scoring, loss and optimizer; retain one model per category.",
  "3": "Training strategy: in all four categories, multiply the current learning rate by 0.8 throughout training, preserving the optimizer type and existing scheduler's relative schedule. A modest reduction may stabilize validation ranking where loss keeps falling after HR@10 peaks. Preserve batch size, dropout, weight decay, model, features, scoring/readout, loss and sampling. Keep training seed 42, preprocessing seed 0 and epoch cap 200; select one checkpoint per category."
